# /web/lib is a library directory, not a document tree. Nothing under it is
# ever fetched over HTTP - it is only ever include()d by PHP that lives
# elsewhere - so serving any of it is a mistake by definition, and 403 is the
# correct answer to a request for one of these paths.
#
# Belt and braces on top of the docroot rules, which already deny
# mysql_config*.php and db_credentials.php by name: this denies the whole
# directory, so a file added here later is covered without anyone having to
# remember to add its name to the vhost.
Require all denied
